Integrity convention (from CZ-IR 1.0, sections 10.4 and 10.5) — a conformance
convention of this project, not a restriction on the licence: CC BY 4.0 alone
governs what anyone may do with these texts. A version, amendment, or translation
that calls itself conforming to the Core preserves its version identifier,
publication date, change history, contributors, reasons for change, evidence
relied upon, and unresolved objections, and states how it maps to the Core. This
project replaces no origin silently: CZ-CORE 1.0 remains permanently accessible in
its original form.
